.TH TALLYDESKLET 1 "October 2026" "TallyDesklet" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tallydesklet \- compact desktop system monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tallydesklet
.RB [ --settings | --reset-position | --quit | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows CPU, RAM, filesystem capacity and throughput on one routed network
interface. Designed for Xfce on X11. Launching again opens preferences.
.SH DATA USAGE
Weekly usage appears left and daily usage right above Network. Totals combine
download and upload on the selected interface while the app runs. Daily totals
reset at local midnight; weekly totals reset Sunday at local midnight.
Totals persist across normal restarts. Traffic while closed and ambiguous
reconnect/reset or sampling-gap traffic is excluded. Initial periods may be partial.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --settings
Open the preferences dialog.
.TP
.B --reset-position
Restore the widget to the primary monitor's upper-right work area.
.TP
.B --quit
Quit the running instance.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version without opening a display.
.SH FILES
.PP
Legacy mint-meter preferences and usage are copied on first launch only if
the corresponding TallyDesklet file is absent. Original files are preserved.
The mint-meter command remains available for compatibility. Quit the old app
before upgrading.
.PP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tallydesklet/config.json
(defaults to ~/.config/tallydesklet/config.json).
.PP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/tallydesklet/usage.json
(defaults to ~/.local/state/tallydesklet/usage.json). At most seven daily totals;
checkpointed once per minute and on normal exit.
.SH NOTES
Startup at login is opt-in. Package removal retains personal settings and
the user autostart entry; disable startup in preferences before removal.
